<title>USA: DuPont Merck unit launches cancer diagnostic test.</title>
<headline>DuPont Merck unit launches cancer diagnostic test.</headline>
<dateline>NORTH BILLERICA, Mass. 1997-02-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>DuPont Merck Pharmaceutical Co said on Monday its Radiopharmaceuticals division began marketing the new Verluma diagnostic test for small-cell lung cancer.</p>
<p>Verluma, a monoclonal antibody-based diagnostic imaging agent recently cleared by the Food and Drug Administration, is intended to reduce the need for some traditional tests in certain circumstances.</p>
<p>DuPont Merck is a partnership between DuPont Co and Merck &amp; Co Inc.</p>
<p>Verluma was developed by NeoRx Corp.</p>
</text>
